  "details": "1. Create an Excellent avatar in Unity Editor\n\n2. Add N particle systems (can be disabled), set its max particles to 0\n\n3. Check the performance estimate in VRChat SDK builder, notice the performance rating is Excellent\n\n4. Upload and check the performance ranking of the uploaded avatar, it'll be Good or worse as the particle systems are counted on the server\n\nAffected avatar: [Robot （0 max particles）](https://vrchat.com/home/avatar/avtr_e785d1e7-6121-4e73-99bd-4bae65e24636) (`avtr_e785d1e7-6121-4e73-99bd-4bae65e24636`) by WubTheCaptain - this has N=1\n\nExpected result: Overall Performance Estimate: Good (or worse) in SDK for having > 0 particle systems.\n\nActual result: Overall Performance Estimate: Excellent in SDK, Excellent in local SDK test avatar (0 particle systems, 0 max particles), Good performance ranking once uploaded to VRChat.\n\nIf you change the max particles on one particle system to 1, the SDK will immediately report \"Good\" as intended.\n\nAdditional information: VRChat SDK - Avatars 3.10.4.",
